PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Round-2 record sustains 20+/22 consensus on B as sole inaccurate statement (Markus develops asymmetry inside—not apart from—post-396 operative grace/predestination in Saeculum and anti-Pelagian essays; “while ignoring” clause is direct factual misrepresentation). All other options remain aligned with primary texts (De lib. arb., Confessiones, anti-Pelagian corpus, Evodius dialogues) and post-Vatican II readings (proto-Calvinist motifs, Gilson’s qualified irresistibility, philosophy/theology inseparability, Stoic coloring of bona voluntas). 

New dissent: Colleagues 7 & 9 flag possible weakness in C (Seneca parallel may be mediated via wider Stoic-Neoplatonic milieu rather than direct “part of psyche” echo; voluntas presented as self-moving inclination of whole rational soul). Colleague 9 explicitly shifts vote to C. Majority rebuttal treats this as interpretive nuance still compatible with standard secondary literature; does not rise to level of error in B. 

No other shifts or new evidence. Persistent minor outlier on A (overstated “creation-fixed destiny”) noted but unchanged. Unresolved question: exact strength of Seneca link in C, but insufficient to displace B. Retain prior evidence convergence on B.}

